i'm a spokesperson said that kakuenza  ruchira bashaija says this is the price  he paid for criticizing uganda's ruling  family he says his ordeal began in  december when soldiers broke into his  house beat him tied him and blindfolded  him before driving him to a military  barracks i don't know what they were  using to beat me in the back either  hippopotamus whip or  a wire  something that really  gets  into the skin it was very painful  excruciating pain  he was detained for four weeks he says  he saw and heard several other prisoners  being tortured too including one man  whose skin was repeatedly burned with an  iron he says the interrogations were  brutal getting  a pliers they start plucking flesh from  my thighs all of this  he believes he was arrested because of  the two books he's published the first  was a satirical critique of uganda's  president yuri museveni and he says he  was detained and tortured for it two  years ago  he described what happened in the second  book the ugandan government denies  running torture chambers this matter is  being investigated by government  within the security circles  but it's not true for him to say  that people who are detained in uganda  are tortured  it is not true to say that there is no  freedom of speech in uganda  president museveni has ruled uganda for  36 years his regime has faced growing  accusations of rights abuses  it's his son general mohozie kainarugaba  that kukuenza blames for his detention  and torture mahouzy denies it and says  he's never met kacuenza  bukakuenza says mahosi saw him three  times during his detention  forced him to apologize made threats and  offered him money to take his books  offline and stop writing that is when i  met  general mahouzy for the third time  and he was like  he wanted to be sure  whether if i am released i am not going  to write another book about my torture  cacuenza was taken to court last month  and charged with insulting the ruling  family the court kept his passport but  he fled to germany where he says he  plans to write another book documenting  what happened to him they have the money  they have the guns but  they touch the wrong battle  they joke with the power of a pain  he says he's so traumatized he can  barely sleep for more than an hour  before being woken by nightmares  he says he'll seek medical treatment in  germany but plans to return to uganda  and continue writing  malcolm webb al jazeera
 

